// check: refuse E_EffectMismatch
// The why verb through an answering arm: `quiet` declares `!WASI` and
// performs only `print`, so its own row never names WASI, but the
// `stdout_console` install in `main` answers that print with a write to the
// host. The check refuses `quiet` with the path through the arm, and
// `mentl why` on quiet and WASI prints that same path.
import io

fn quiet() with !WASI = print("hi\n")

fn main() = quiet() ~> stdout_console
